  "grammar": {
    "title": "Separable verbs: opstaan → ik sta op",
    "points": [
      "Some verbs start with a prefix that can split off: opstaan (op + staan), opbellen, meenemen, terugkomen, thuiskomen.",
      "In a normal sentence the verb takes second place and the prefix goes to the very end: Ik sta om zeven uur op.",
      "With a modal verb or gaan, the verb stays in one piece at the end: Ik moet vroeg opstaan.",
      "The stress is on the prefix: OPstaan, MEEnemen.",
      "Words like eerst, dan and daarna at the start of a sentence still keep the verb in second place: Daarna douche ik."
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "nl": "Ik sta om zeven uur op.", "en": "I get up at seven." },
      { "nl": "Sara neemt haar lunch mee.", "en": "Sara brings her lunch." },
      { "nl": "Om zes uur kom ik thuis.", "en": "I get home at six." },
      { "nl": "Ik bel mijn moeder op.", "en": "I call my mother." },
      { "nl": "Ik moet morgen vroeg opstaan.", "en": "I have to get up early tomorrow." }
    ],
